  "scientific_result": "Across the 2 post-occlusion physical-state variables probed (post_occlusion_position_x, post_occlusion_velocity_x), evaluated with an identical scene set, scene-level train/test split, encoder, pooling, and linear ridge probe: 2/2 variables showed the post-occlusion representation's real probe exceeding the object-identity-scrambled control (post_occlusion_position_x, post_occlusion_velocity_x). This is evidence that the frozen representation's post-occlusion window carries linearly-recoverable information about the tracked object's physical state beyond a chance/scrambled-identity level, for this occlusion pattern and scene distribution -- an accessibility/persistence finding, not evidence of an internal object model (DESIGN.md Sec 13; tasks/13_occlusion.md's interpretation limits).\n\nPer-variable detail:\n- post_occlusion_position_x: post-occlusion real probe R^2=-0.007 vs. scrambled-identity control R^2=-0.359 (mean baseline R^2=-0.022); no_occlusion upper bound R^2=0.057; real probe exceeded the scrambled-identity control.\n- post_occlusion_velocity_x: post-occlusion real probe R^2=-0.007 vs. scrambled-identity control R^2=-0.359 (mean baseline R^2=-0.022); no_occlusion upper bound R^2=0.057; real probe exceeded the scrambled-identity control.",
